      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Watering style is a mapping: Clemson 'water when dry 2-3 in down' sits between top-dry and fully-dry; let_top_dry stored as the cautious value. Toxicity: NC State tag and the ASPCA page agree (non-toxic for cats and dogs). Interval: Clemson 'water when dry 2-3 in down' (earlier read); NC State 'water regularly spring to autumn, sparingly in winter', drought tolerant; Missouri Botanical Garden 'water regularly spring to fall, reduce in winter', 'will tolerate less regular watering'. Two to three inches down in a 13 cm pot is most of the pot, about 10 days, so 10 (unchanged). Pot and season: 13 cm pot, bright indirect light, room temperature, growing season. Dry and wet tolerance days: no source gives days, left as before."
      },
